# Run the verification loop

## Commands
| Goal | Command |
|---|---|
| Is my toolchain ready? | `./scripts/sdlc doctor` then `./scripts/sdlc setup` |
| Fast feedback while coding | `./scripts/sdlc gates` (or `--only <gate-id>`, `--stage unit`) |
| Prove acceptance criteria on the running system | `./scripts/sdlc facts` |
| Everything CI runs | `./scripts/sdlc verify` |
| Verify, heal, verify until green | `./scripts/sdlc loop` |
| Spec in, verified code out (agent writes it) | `./scripts/sdlc implement FEAT-xxx` (`--dry-run` shows the prompt first) |
| One feature incl. PRD drafting and deploy | `./scripts/sdlc feature FEAT-xxx` |
| Install dependencies after editing a manifest | `./scripts/sdlc sync` |
| Read the last result | `./scripts/sdlc report` |

## Reading the result
- `PASS`/`FAIL` per gate and per check. `WARN` = non-required gate failed (audit): report it, don't hide it. `SKIP` = capability missing in this runtime: *not verified*.
- Evidence lives in `.ai/evidence/latest/`: `report.md` (human), `results.json` (machine), `logs/<id>.log` (full output).
- The traceability table shows each AC -> checks -> status. A feature is done only when all its ACs are PASS.

## Exit codes
`0` verified · `1` failed (or out of iterations) · `2` needs a human (no agent configured / PRD stub) · `3` same failure repeated, no progress · `4` integrity violation (protected files changed).

## Rules
- Trust the report, not your memory. Re-run after any change.
- A stage failing stops the run (failFast). Fix, re-run; later stages run once earlier ones pass.
- Never report "verified" for anything the report shows as SKIP or FAIL.
